  "overview_markdown": "OpenFang positions itself not as a chatbot framework but as a full **Agent Operating System** written from scratch in Rust — roughly 137K lines of code across 14 crates, compiling to a single ~32MB binary. Its core differentiator is **Hands**: pre-built autonomous capability packages that run on schedules without user prompting, handling tasks like competitor research, knowledge-graph building, lead generation, and social media management, with results surfaced through a local dashboard on port 4200.\n\nArchitecturally, it contrasts sharply with OpenClaw's chat-centric model. Where OpenClaw is a personal assistant you text through WhatsApp/Telegram/Slack, OpenFang agents run 24/7 in the background and report to a dashboard. The project touts strong engineering hygiene — 2,696+ passing tests and zero clippy warnings — and recent commits show security-focused work (audit fixes, TOCTOU hardening, endpoint audits).\n\nThe main caveats are maturity and momentum. OpenFang is explicitly pre-1.0 with breaking changes between minor versions, and a third-party liveness review flagged its last release as May 2026 (v0.6.9), suggesting development may have slowed. It also lacks OpenClaw's multi-channel messaging integrations and its large community skills registry, making it a better fit for autonomous back-office automation than for conversational personal-assistant use.",
